ity different from a single population?","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[51],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_BIOLOGY_LSC_level-1and-2_-Final-2024-Web-file_Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-biology-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 2","title":"Locomotion in Mammals","summary":"Mammalian movement depends on coordinated action between muscles, bones and joints.","learning_outcomes":["Identify parts of the skeleton and explain how muscle action produces movement."],"study_sections":[{"content":"Mammalian movement depends on coordinated action between muscles, bones and joints.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Identify parts of the skeleton and explain how muscle action produces movement.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"Why must muscles and the skeleton work together?","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[37],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_BIOLOGY_LSC_level-1and-2_-Final-2024-Web-file_Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-biology-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 2","title":"Nervous Coordination in Humans","summary":"The nervous system carries signals between receptors, processing centres and effectors to coordinate responses.","learning_outcomes":["Identify major components and trace a simple response pathway; consider how some chemicals can disrupt signalling."],"study_sections":[{"content":"The nervous system carries signals between receptors, processing centres and effectors to coordinate responses.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Identify major components and trace a simple response pathway; consider how some chemicals can disrupt signalling.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"What role does a receptor play in a response pathway?","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[34],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_BIOLOGY_LSC_level-1and-2_-Final-2024-Web-file_Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-biology-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 2","title":"Receptor Organs in Man","summary":"Sensory organs such as the eye and ear detect stimuli and help the body respond to its surroundings.","learning_outcomes":["Identify important eye and ear structures and connect each to its function."],"study_sections":[{"content":"Sensory organs such as the eye and ear detect stimuli and help the body respond to its surroundings.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Identify important eye and ear structures and connect each to its function.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"What type of stimulus is detected by the ear?","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[36],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_BIOLOGY_LSC_level-1and-2_-Final-2024-Web-file_Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-biology-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 2","title":"Sexual Reproduction in Human","summary":"Human sexual reproduction involves specialised reproductive systems and reproductive cells from two parents.","learning_outcomes":["Identify major reproductive structures and describe the basic purpose of reproductive cells."],"study_sections":[{"content":"Human sexual reproduction involves specialised reproductive systems and reproductive cells from two parents.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Identify major reproductive structures and describe the basic purpose of reproductive cells.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"Why are reproductive cells specialised?","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[46],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_BIOLOGY_LSC_level-1and-2_-Final-2024-Web-file_Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-biology-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 2","title":"Sexual Reproduction in Plants","summary":"Flowers are specialised structures for sexual reproduction in flowering plants, leading to seed formation and an embryo.","learning_outcomes":["Identify flower structures and connect pollination and fertilisation to seed formation."],"study_sections":[{"content":"Flowers are specialised structures for sexual reproduction in flowering plants, leading to seed formation and an embryo.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Identify flower structures and connect pollination and fertilisation to seed formation.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"What role does a flower play in sexual reproduction?","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[44],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_BIOLOGY_LSC_level-1and-2_-Final-2024-Web-file_Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-physics-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 1","title":"Earth and Space Physics","summary":"The relative positions and movements of the Sun, Earth and Moon help explain observable events; the topic also introduces solar systems, stars and galaxies.","learning_outcomes":["Use labelled models to explain relative movement and distinguish our Solar System from the wider universe."],"study_sections":[{"content":"The relative positions and movements of the Sun, Earth and Moon help explain observable events; the topic also introduces solar systems, stars and galaxies.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Use labelled models to explain relative movement and distinguish our Solar System from the wider universe.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"How can a model help explain the relative movement of Earth and the Moon?","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[22],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_PHYSICS_LSC_level-1and-2.pdf_Web-file-Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-physics-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 1","title":"Forces and their Effects","summary":"Forces can change an object''s motion, direction or shape; this topic also connects forces with turning effects, work, energy, motion and pressure.","learning_outcomes":["Compare force types and use practical examples to explain their effects on objects."],"study_sections":[{"content":"Forces can change an object''s motion, direction or shape; this topic also connects forces with turning effects, work, energy, motion and pressure.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Compare force types and use practical examples to explain their effects on objects.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"Give one example of a force changing an object''s motion or shape.","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[5],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_PHYSICS_LSC_level-1and-2.pdf_Web-file-Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-physics-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 1","title":"Light","summary":"Light behaves differently when it meets different materials and boundaries, and these behaviours support useful applications.","learning_outcomes":["Investigate how light travels and interacts with materials, then relate observations to practical uses."],"study_sections":[{"content":"Light behaves differently when it meets different materials and boundaries, and these behaviours support useful applications.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Investigate how light travels and interacts with materials, then relate observations to practical uses.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"What observation could help explain the behaviour of light at a boundary?","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[15],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_PHYSICS_LSC_level-1and-2.pdf_Web-file-Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-physics-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 1","title":"Measurements","summary":"Measurements describe quantities such as length, mass, time, volume and density using numerical readings and suitable units.","learning_outcomes":["Choose a suitable instrument and unit, read scales carefully, and record results with units."],"study_sections":[{"content":"Measurements describe quantities such as length, mass, time, volume and density using numerical readings and suitable units.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Choose a suitable instrument and unit, read scales carefully, and record results with units.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"Why is a unit necessary when recording a measurement?","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[2],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_PHYSICS_LSC_level-1and-2.pdf_Web-file-Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-physics-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 1","title":"Waves","summary":"Waves transfer energy, and transverse and longitudinal waves differ in how their oscillations relate to the direction of travel.","learning_outcomes":["Identify basic wave properties and compare wave types, including sound."],"study_sections":[{"content":"Waves transfer energy, and transverse and longitudinal waves differ in how their oscillations relate to the direction of travel.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Identify basic wave properties and compare wave types, including sound.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"How do transverse and longitudinal waves differ?","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[18],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_PHYSICS_LSC_level-1and-2.pdf_Web-file-Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-physics-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 2","title":"Atomic and Nuclear Physics","summary":"Atomic and nuclear physics introduces atomic particles and structure alongside cathode rays, X-rays and radioactivity.","learning_outcomes":["Describe the main particles in an atom and distinguish the topic areas covered in this unit."],"study_sections":[{"content":"Atomic and nuclear physics introduces atomic particles and structure alongside cathode rays, X-rays and radioactivity.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Describe the main particles in an atom and distinguish the topic areas covered in this unit.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"Name the main particles found in an atom.","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[48],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_PHYSICS_LSC_level-1and-2.pdf_Web-file-Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-physics-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 2","title":"Digital Electronics","summary":"Digital electronics studies how electronic components are combined into circuits that carry out useful functions.","learning_outcomes":["Recognise circuit components and relate their arrangement to the operation of simple digital systems."],"study_sections":[{"content":"Digital electronics studies how electronic components are combined into circuits that carry out useful functions.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Recognise circuit components and relate their arrangement to the operation of simple digital systems.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"Why does the arrangement of circuit components matter?","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[53],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_PHYSICS_LSC_level-1and-2.pdf_Web-file-Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-physics-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 2","title":"Electricity and Magnetism","summary":"Electricity and magnetism includes static charge, current electricity, practical electrical systems, magnets, electromagnets and induction.","learning_outcomes":["Compare static and current electricity, identify magnetic effects and connect these ideas to devices and safe practice."],"study_sections":[{"content":"Electricity and magnetism includes static charge, current electricity, practical electrical systems, magnets, electromagnets and induction.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Compare static and current electricity, identify magnetic effects and connect these ideas to devices and safe practice.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"State one difference between static and current electricity.","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[36],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_PHYSICS_LSC_level-1and-2.pdf_Web-file-Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-physics-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 2","title":"Satellites and Communication","summary":"Artificial satellites support communication, observation and space exploration by operating above Earth for specific purposes.","learning_outcomes":["Identify satellite applications and explain how they can support communication or observation."],"study_sections":[{"content":"Artificial satellites support communication, observation and space exploration by operating above Earth for specific purposes.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Identify satellite applications and explain how they can support communication or observation.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"Give one application of an artificial satellite.","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[52],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_PHYSICS_LSC_level-1and-2.pdf_Web-file-Final-08.03.2024.pdf"},{"source_document_id":"ncdc-aep-physics-lsc-level-1-2-2023","level_label":"Level 2","title":"Thermal Physics","summary":"The kinetic model uses particle arrangement and motion to explain matter in solid, liquid, gas and plasma states.","learning_outcomes":["Connect particle behaviour to temperature, heat transfer, expansion and heat quantities."],"study_sections":[{"content":"The kinetic model uses particle arrangement and motion to explain matter in solid, liquid, gas and plasma states.","heading":"Core idea"},{"content":"Connect particle behaviour to temperature, heat transfer, expansion and heat quantities.","heading":"Study focus"},{"content":"How does particle motion help explain a property of gases?","heading":"Check your understanding"}],"source_pages":[28],"source_url":"https://ncdc.go.ug/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NCDC_AEP_PHYSICS_LSC_level-1and-2.pdf_Web-file-Final-08.03.2024.pdf"}]'::jsonb) as x(
    source_document_id text,
    level_label text,
    title text,
    summary text,
    learning_outcomes jsonb,
    study_sections jsonb,
    source_pages integer[],
    source_url text
  )
)
insert into public.curriculum_document_notes
(source_document_id,source_topic_id,subject_label,programme,level_label,title,summary,learning_outcomes,study_sections,source_pages,source_url,review_status,publication_status)
select d.id,t.id,d.subject_label,d.curriculum_programme,s.level_label,s.title,s.summary,
       s.learning_outcomes,s.study_sections,s.source_pages,s.source_url,'in_review','draft'
from seed s
join public.curriculum_documents d on d.id=s.source_document_id
join public.curriculum_document_topics t
  on t.source_document_id=d.id and t.level_label=s.level_label and t.title=s.title
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.curriculum_document_notes existing
  where existing.source_topic_id=t.id
);
